# orch CODEOWNERS lines — TEMPLATE shipped with orch-gate.
#
# What it does: makes the orch boundaries reviewable only by their owners. The
# registry, contracts, planning artifacts and the orch-gate CLI decide what a
# PR may touch, and the CI files decide which CLI judges it. A PR runs its own
# copy of the CI file (`.github/workflows/orch-gate.yml`, or
# `.gitlab/orch-gate.gitlab-ci.yml` and `.gitlab-ci.yml`), so the gate's
# "CLI comes from the base" rule holds only when those files are code-owned and
# the `orch-gate` job is required. A PR that updates orch is gated by the old
# version, and these owners review it.
#
# Installation: orch-setup SUGGESTS these lines and never writes them. The
# user adds them to the CODEOWNERS file the platform actually reads, merging
# with any existing entries; never clobber that file. Each platform uses the
# first file it finds: GitHub `.github/CODEOWNERS`, then `CODEOWNERS`, then
# `docs/CODEOWNERS`; GitLab `CODEOWNERS`, then `docs/CODEOWNERS`, then
# `.gitlab/CODEOWNERS`. Every location is owned below, so a PR cannot add a
# higher-priority file that shadows these lines without the orch owners.
# - Substitute every placeholder with a path relative to the repo root (never
#   an absolute path or a project-root / skill-root variable):
#   `@ORCH_REGISTRY_DIR@` (default `_bmad-output/orch/subprojects`),
#   `@ORCH_CONTRACTS_DIR@` (default `_bmad-output/orch/contracts`),
#   `@PLANNING_ARTIFACTS@` (default `_bmad-output/planning-artifacts`),
#   `@ORCH_CLI_DIR@` (default `.claude/skills/orch-gate`), and `@ORCH_OWNERS@`
#   with the owning users or teams (e.g. `@org/orch-owners`).
# - `_bmad/config.toml` and `_bmad/custom/config.toml` set the registry,
#   contracts and planning paths the gate reads, so they are owned too.
# - Required checks match by name and GitLab local includes can redefine job
#   keys: also own all of `/.github/workflows/` and every CI file that
#   `.gitlab-ci.yml` includes, or a PR can add a look-alike passing job.
# - Lines for the platform not in use are harmless and may be dropped. Later
#   CODEOWNERS lines win, so put these after broader patterns.
# - Turn on required code-owner review for the main branch (GitHub: "Require
#   review from Code Owners"; GitLab: code-owner approval on the protected
#   branch, which needs GitLab Premium or higher) and require the `orch-gate`
#   job (GitHub: also in the merge queue; GitLab: not under merge trains).
# - This protects a monorepo whose registry lists only `repo: .`; a registry
#   with other repos needs the polyrepo follow-up.
/@ORCH_REGISTRY_DIR@/ @ORCH_OWNERS@
/@ORCH_CONTRACTS_DIR@/ @ORCH_OWNERS@
/@PLANNING_ARTIFACTS@/ @ORCH_OWNERS@
/@ORCH_CLI_DIR@/ @ORCH_OWNERS@
/.github/workflows/orch-gate.yml @ORCH_OWNERS@
/.gitlab/orch-gate.gitlab-ci.yml @ORCH_OWNERS@
/.gitlab-ci.yml @ORCH_OWNERS@
/_bmad/config.toml @ORCH_OWNERS@
/_bmad/custom/config.toml @ORCH_OWNERS@
/.github/CODEOWNERS @ORCH_OWNERS@
/CODEOWNERS @ORCH_OWNERS@
/docs/CODEOWNERS @ORCH_OWNERS@
/.gitlab/CODEOWNERS @ORCH_OWNERS@
